# Fixed 2026-10-02, defect 135's class, lane literals (the certain-fix
# audit's L5, and the shapes beside it). Symptom: `0X`, `0B` or `0O` with no
# digit after it cost `base_prefix_case` with the certain fix that lowers
# the prefix, so `check --apply` wrote `0x`, which costs
# `empty_base_literal`: a refusal the first run never made, a second turn
# for one literal. Cause: the lowering was certain whatever followed the
# prefix. Now it is certain only where a digit of the base follows, or where
# the digits faulted and the first run told it; with no digit at all the one
# diagnostic says the literal also stops, its note names the digits it
# needs, no fix is offered, and `--apply` leaves the case as it is
# (`number.hero`).

function each_base()
    print(0X)  #~ base_prefix_case
    print(0B)  #~ base_prefix_case
    print(0O)  #~ base_prefix_case

function inside_brackets_and_before_an_operator()
    xs = [0X, 1]  #~ base_prefix_case
    print(xs.len() + 0B + 1)  #~ base_prefix_case

function in_a_pattern()
    k = match 0
        0X => 1  #~ base_prefix_case
        _ => 2
    print(k)

constant EMPTY: i64
    #~v base_prefix_case
    0O
